<title>BELGIUM: EU seeks to agree meat deal with U.S. - Fischler.</title>
<headline>EU seeks to agree meat deal with U.S. - Fischler.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union Farm Commissioner said on Wednesday that the EU and the U.S. were trying to agree on meat hygiene inspection rules today.</p>
<p>&quot;We are to try and bring negotiations to a positive outcome,&quot; Fischler told a news conference, reporting on a telephone conversation with U.S. Secretary of Agriculture Dan Glickman on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There are still talks to be held and I don't want to prejudice the outcome,&quot; he added.</p>
<p>Fischler said it was important to end the negotiations on Wednesday because an extended U.S. deadline for blocking imports of EU meat expires on April 30.</p>
<p>&quot;To keep postponing the deadline does not make much sense,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Fischler declined to speculate on whether an eventual veterinary equivalency agreement would include poultry -- the main outstanding obstacle.</p>
<p>The EU says that the U.S. method of decontaminating chicken carcasses in chlorinated water is unacceptable.</p>
<p>-Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
</text>
